<td>3-7 business days</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Complex account structure issues</td>
<td>7-15 business days</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>If you haven't received a response after 15 business days, contact Google Ads support through official channels (like Twitter @GoogleAds) and reference your submission date.</p>
<h2>What Can You Do If Your Appeal Is Rejected?</h2>
<p>A rejected appeal isn't the end of the road:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Submit supplementary materials</strong>: Address the specific rejection reason with new evidence</li>
<li><strong>Escalate through official channels</strong>: In support conversations, explicitly request escalation to a specialized team</li>
<li><strong>Check for associated account risks</strong>: If other accounts under the same IP or payment method have issues, a comprehensive audit may be necessary</li>
</ul>
<p>What you shouldn't do: repeatedly submit identical appeal materials. This gets flagged by the system as无效提交, reducing your chances of success on future attempts.</p>
<h2>How to Reduce the Risk of Future Suspensions?</h2>
<p>Winning an appeal is just the first step. Maintaining account health is what matters long-term.</p>
<p><strong>Daily operational recommendations:</strong><br />
- Review ad copy and landing pages monthly for policy compliance<br />
- Use corporate bank accounts for payments to avoid credit card churn triggering risk controls<br />
- If managing multiple accounts, ensure no shared payment information or attribution links between them</p>
<p>Account suspension isn't the end—it's an opportunity to build better prevention mechanisms. If you have questions about account appeals or overseas advertising, contact 以渔数媒 for further support.</p>
